      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "U11 pins 13 and 14 (LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX-) are connected to the GND net.",
      "expected": "These Ethernet PHY transmit pins should not be tied to ground; in the reference design they are unconnected or used as GPIO, but not shorted to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the SKW92A's Ethernet PHY is active, grounding its transmit outputs can cause excessive current, damage the PHY, or prevent proper operation. Even if unused, it is a short.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C7"],
      "pins": ["C7.1", "C7.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(U1-K)", "Net-(Q2-D)"],
      "observed": "C7 has value 4.7uF/25V.",
      "expected": "C7 should be 1uF/25V per the PDI reference and spec.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C7\") (value \"4.7uF/25V\")"}
      ],
      "impact": "Changes the EPD charge-pump capacitance, potentially altering the boost converter's voltage regulation and timing, which could cause the e-paper display to malfunction.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "footprint_mismatch",
      "components": ["C13"],
      "pins": ["C13.1", "C13.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C13-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C13 is a 0.1uF capacitor with footprint 'Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder' and pin 1 is unconnected.",
      "expected": "A capacitor should use a capacitor footprint, and the spec's C13 is a 10uF output capacitor (though the netlist uses C9 for that role). This extra component is not properly connected.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C13\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C13-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"C13\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If assembled, a capacitor on an inductor footprint may not fit or may be placed incorrectly. Since it is unconnected, it has no electrical effect, but it indicates a design/assembly error.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a serious short-to-ground on the SKW92A Ethernet transmit pins U11.13/U11.14, a wrong value for EPD charge-pump capacitor C7 (4.7uF instead of 1uF), and a footprint mismatch on C13. The first two are likely to affect board behavior."
}

